text:
Hi;

I grew up on Persian food in LA. OK not only that, but I think I have a good taste for it and quality. I am giving 4 stars as they are the best in the East Bay Area I found. There is a great place in Marin, but nothing like LA!

I think the portion sizes are simply too big. Save some of the value and out that in garnish and extras is my only feedback to them....

All I have to say is that this place has effectively rekindled a boba addiction. 

Lady's kinda mean though! I'm sorry a Mexican decided to come in. Well actually, I think it was the fact that I was clueless and my boyfriend wasn't that made her be kind of rude. I'm not Asian I swear ;_;
I experience this a lot.

this place is open late for the drunkards

for three dollars you get a delicious hot dog on a perfectly toasted bun (real buns not the skimpy generic buns that come in packs of 16 at the store)

WARNING: one of the mustards has wasabi or something in it and it's intensely spicy and can ruin your dog! I thought I was up for the challenge I THOUGHT WRONG. avoid this mustard or only use small doses
